###
Addon syntax.

Every line below belongs to an addon, not to core Skript. What you see depends
on what your server actually has installed:

  * addon installed  — hover, completion and colour, same as core syntax
  * addon missing    — the line stays plain, and says nothing

That silence is deliberate. There are 168 addons and 12,877 patterns published;
guessing would mean a wall of false errors on every real server.

To see the difference, point the server at a real server directory:

  "lsp": { "skript-lsp": { "initialization_options": {
    "serverPath": "/srv/minecraft/my-server"
  } } }
###

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- SkBee (NBT)

on rightclick with a stick:
	set {_nbt} to nbt compound of event-block
	if {_nbt} is a blank nbt compound:
		send "no data" to player
		stop
	set {_id} to tag "minecraft:custom" of {_nbt}
	send "%{_id}%" to player

# --------------------------------------------------------- SkBee (structures)

on load:
	set {_creator} to a new world creator named "lobby"
	set {_bound} to bound between {_a} and {_b}

# ----------------------------------------------------- skript-reflect (import)

import:
	java.util.UUID
	org.bukkit.Bukkit

on script load:
	set {_version} to Bukkit.getVersion()

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- unknown

# Syntax from an addon nothing knows about. It parses — indentation, strings and
# variables are all still structural — but it is never reported as an error.
on some undocumented addon event:
	do the undocumented thing with {_x}
